      "id": "sol.ahsme-1973-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sequence is \\[ 51,61,\\ldots,341. \\] It has \\[ \\frac{341-51}{10}+1=30 \\] terms. Its sum is therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\frac{30(51+341)}2 &=15\\cdot392\\\\ &=5880. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
